Catalogue, TUI editing, presets under ~/.grok, user docs and changelog.

Carried into the patch queue so it survives upstream syncs. It was written
directly on the 1.0.0 sync branch with no Gork-Patch-Id trailer, so it was
never exported to maint/patches — and `patchctl apply` rebuilds the branch
from upstream plus the queue alone. The 1.0.1 repatch dropped it silently.

Marked critical for the same reason: a trailing non-critical patch is
skipped on conflict, which would repeat that silent loss. A conflict here
must stop the sync and be ported by hand.

Ported to 1.0.3 with two conflicts, both trivial: `prompt/mod.rs` (upstream
added `browser_verification` next to this patch's `catalog`; both kept) and
the shell CHANGELOG (the Unreleased section now sits above 1.0.1-1.0.3).

Gork-Patch-Id: prompts-modal
Gork-Risk: low
